#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:22
msgid "Contours"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:24
msgid ""
"The :meth:`pygmt.Figure.contour` method can plot contour lines from a table "
"of points by direct triangulation. The data for the triangulation can be "
"provided using one of three methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:28
msgid "``x``, ``y``, ``z`` 1-D :class:`numpy.ndarray` data columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:29
msgid ""
"``data`` 2-D :class:`numpy.ndarray` data matrix with 3 columns corresponding "
"to ``x``, ``y``, ``z``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:31
msgid ""
"``data`` path string to a file containing the ``x``, ``y``, ``z`` in a "
"tabular format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:34
msgid ""
"The parameters ``levels`` and ``annotation`` set the intervals of the "
"contours and the annotations on the contours, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:37
msgid ""
"In this example we supply the data as 1-D :class:`numpy.ndarray` with the "
"``x``, ``y``, and ``z`` parameters and draw the contours using a 0.5-points "
"pen with contours every 10 z-values and annotations every 20 z-values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/images/contours.rst:43
msgid ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis\n"
"\n"
"# Build the contours underlying data with the function z = x^2 + y^2\n"
"X, Y = np.meshgrid(np.linspace(-10, 10, 50), np.linspace(-10, 10, 50))\n"
"Z = X**2 + Y**2\n"
"x, y, z = X.flatten(), Y.flatten(), Z.flatten()\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.contour(\n"
"    region=[-10, 10, -10, 10],\n"
"    projection=\"X10c/10c\",\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True, grid=True),\n"
"    pen=\"0.5p\",\n"
"    # Pass the data as 3 1-D data columns\n"
"    x=x,\n"
"    y=y,\n"
"    z=z,\n"
"    # Set the interval of the contours to 10\n"
"    levels=10,\n"
"    # Set the interval of the annotations to 20\n"
"    annotation=20,\n"
")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

